<article class="env-exercise" id="028K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/028K">Exercise <span data-tag="028K">111.30.13</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an abelian category. Consider a solid diagram </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ K^\bullet \ar[r]_\alpha \ar[d]_\gamma &  L^\bullet \ar@{-->}[dl]^{\beta _ i} \\  I^\bullet }  \]
</div>
  <p> of complexes of $\text{Fil}^ f(\mathcal{A})$. Assume $K^\bullet $, $L^\bullet $ and $I^\bullet $ bounded below and each $I^ n$ a filtered injective object. Also assume $\alpha $ a filtered quasi-isomorphism. Any two morphisms $\beta _1, \beta _2$ making the diagram commute up to homotopy are homotopic. </p>
</article>